# Frontend Docker Build Context Exclusions
#
# WHY THIS FILE MATTERS (Build Speed Issue)
# ------------------------------------------
# node_modules can be 200–400MB. Without .dockerignore, Docker sends the
# entire node_modules to the build daemon on every `docker-compose build`.
#
# The Dockerfile already runs `npm install` inside the container, so
# sending your local node_modules is not only wasteful — it can also cause
# platform mismatches (e.g., local macOS native binaries in a Linux container).
#
# FIX: Exclude node_modules and build artifacts. The builder context drops
# from ~300MB to ~50KB, making `docker build` context upload near-instant.

node_modules
dist
.vite

# Git and IDE
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Local env
.env
.env.local

# Docs
*.md
